    "phase": "Phase 6 (session hardening): SESSION_ENGINE = cached_db — the cache is in front of the django_session table. A warm request saves the session SELECT (one fewer DB round trip per request, measured: exactly -1 query on every path, -11 on the 100-row loop); the session write still lands in the table, so a cache flush can never kill a logged-in session, and a dead cache (IGNORE_EXCEPTIONS fail-open) degrades transparently to the plain DB engine. The optional LoginAttempt -> atomic Redis counter stays deferred by design (gated on a real brute-force/scale trigger; the DB lockout, one row per username, touched only by failed logins, behind the Phase-3 global 10/min login throttle, is sufficient at the current scale)."
